{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Yet the one who takes possession:</b> This is the enemy. There is no reason to interpret it as one of the sons of Shem who took possession of the land, namely Elam; rather, it is the enemy who took possession of the land. It is also possible that this prophet was from this city. Do not wonder on account of the change of vowels, that he said היורש in correspondence to מרשה — and the language is not precisely patterned so that this corresponds to that, for nouns are not kept to the same precision as verbs are, since verbs follow a single pattern — like השולמית, which relates to Shalem, which is Jerusalem, when it should have said השלימית." "<b>As far as Adullam:</b> A city in the land of Canaan. And היורש is in place of אחי, and thus it is: 'the glory of Israel is taken possession of.'"], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:39.482224843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}